%% DM26-0670

%% Runtime attestation, slice A: the instance check at issuance (runtime-attestation.md, "The plan"). All designed, nothing built.
%% At issuance a pod is checked against its Deployment; the Deployments are checked against the signed record continually (the maintainer, 2026-11-02).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Init as polar-init (a workload's pod)
    participant Obs as Credentials observer
    participant CA as Credentials agent
    participant Att as Attestation agent
    participant API as Kubernetes API
    participant CI as cert-issuer
    participant Sch as Configuration agent
    participant Repo as Deployment repository, on Polar's git server

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Att,API: DESIGNED: read from what it already holds, not a call per question
    Att->>API: watch pods, ReplicaSets and Deployments in Polar's namespaces (get, list, watch only)
    API-->>Att: every change

    Init->>Obs: issuance request, with the token Kubernetes signed for this pod
    Obs->>CA: the request, over Cassini
    CA->>CA: verify the token, its identity and the pod UID it is bound to, then the renewal rule
    CA->>Att: attestation-instance-requests: this identity, this pod UID

    alt the attestation agent answers
        Att->>Att: the pod exists with that UID
        Att->>Att: its owner chain ends at the Deployment the catalog names for the identity
        Att->>Att: it runs as the expected service account
        Att->>Att: each container's imageID (the kubelet's) is the digest its Deployment pins
        Att->>Att: it has no ephemeral container
        alt all of them hold
            Att-->>CA: Genuine
            CA->>CI: vouch for the certificate
            CI-->>CA: signed
            CA-->>Init: the certificate, through the observer
        else any of them does not
            Att-->>CA: NotGenuine, and why
            CA->>CA: record and log the refusal
            CA-->>Init: refused
        end
    else it cannot be asked (not up, restarting, Cassini down)
        CA->>CI: vouch for the certificate
        CI-->>CA: signed
        CA->>CA: record the issuance as made without attestation
        CA-->>Init: the certificate, through the observer
    end
    end

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Init,CI: DESIGNED: a token-only request in one of the core's windows (a ticket, the crash window, Cassini's route)
    Init->>CI: a bootstrap identity's request, on its token alone
    CI->>CI: is its entry open?
    CI->>Att: attestation-instance-requests, whenever it is reachable
    Att-->>CI: Genuine or NotGenuine: the attestation decides who gets through
    CI-->>Init: signed, or refused. Not reachable: signed, and attested afterwards
    end

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over CI,Att: DESIGNED: what was signed before anything could attest it, and while the agent was away
    Att->>CI: cert-issuer's record: each entry carries its pod UID
    CI-->>Att: the entries
    Att->>CA: the same for the issuances recorded as made without attestation
    CA-->>Att: the entries
    Att->>Att: attest every running pod they name
    Att-)CA: any that fail: the credentials agent, as body guard, stops renewing
    end

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Att,Repo: DESIGNED: the Deployments against the signed record. An issuance waits on none of this
    Repo-->>Sch: a new commit, carrying the deployment's facts as a document the pipeline certificate signed
    Sch-)Att: the document, on the agent's configuration topic. The observer is not trusted
    Att->>Att: verify it to the deployment CA, for this section alone, and apply it
    loop on every change, and on a schedule
        Att->>Att: every Deployment's pins, owner and service account against the document
    end
    Att-)CA: a mismatch: reported, and the credentials agent, as body guard, stops renewing
    end
